      "content": "I see. So if they're basically considered terrorists by international reports, I should probably just stay far away from anyone associated with them. But what about the other side of that conflict? I've heard some people say that the groups being labeled as \"peaceful\" or \"moderate\" by Western media are actually just as aggressive, just more politically savvy. Is there any truth to that, or is it fair to just take the international reports at face value for determining who is actually a threat?",
